mpt Version 5 - Segment 1: 开场亮相叫卖 (6s)]\n\nsubject_definitions:\n<Picture 1> is the four-panel character ID card in 16:9, showing ONE identical middle-aged Sichuan street vendor — face extreme close-up, upper-body front, full-body front, and full-body back — with a round face, warm natural Asian skin tone, and short black hair with slight gray at the temples. ONLY the face and body shape are referenced from <Picture 1>; clothing and the light-gray background are NOT referenced.\n<Subject 1> is the itinerant medicine peddler whose face and body shape come from <Picture 1>: a round-faced middle-aged Sichuan man around 45, warm natural Asian skin tone, short black hair with slight gray at the temples. He wears a faded, dust-stained coarse-woven tan cloth jacket with patched elbows, a loose cloth waistband, rolled trouser legs, and worn straw sandals — a rough, weathered itinerant-peddler look. He holds a woven straw hat in one hand and exactly ONE small herbal liniment bottle in the other. He is the ONLY speaking person, and his lip movements are driven by <Audio 1>. He stands on the ROADSIDE, on the SAME side of the street as the buildings, with the row of old buildings directly behind his back — he must NOT stand in the center of the road.\n<Subject 2> is the customers: EXACTLY SEVEN villagers — middle-aged and elderly men and women in plain worn farm clothes, one or two carrying cloth bags — standing on the road in front of the stall, on the FAR side of <Subject 1>'s goods, directly OPPOSITE him, facing him. They only listen, nod, and murmur softly; they NEVER speak, never cross the stall, and no extra people are added.\n<Subject 3> is the neighboring vendors: EXACTLY TWO other street vendors standing in the SAME vendor row as <Subject 1>, one on his LEFT and one on his RIGHT, also on the roadside with their backs to the same row of buildings, each behind their own small ground stall, tending their goods and calling out softly; they never approach <Subject 1> and ne