 lively street-market atmosphere; no visual effects are added. The spatial layout is fixed throughout and must be kept exactly: the whole vendor row runs along ONE side of the street, pressed against the buildings — <Subject 1> and <Subject 3> all stand on the same roadside, backs against the same row of old buildings, all facing the road together; <Subject 1> must NOT stand in the center of the street; his cloth ground stall lies directly in front of him on the roadside; <Subject 2> stands on the far side of the stall, facing him from the road.\n[Shot 1] A medium shot from the customers' side frames <Subject 1>, the round-faced middle-aged Sichuan peddler from <Picture 1>, standing on the roadside pressed against a row of old brick-and-timber buildings with grey plaster walls, wooden doors, and tiled roofs stretching left and right. In the SAME row on his left and right, <Subject 3>, exactly two neighboring vendors, stand with their backs to the same buildings. Directly in front of <Subject 1>, on the roadside, lies his cloth stall with several bottles, herb bundles, and small earthen jars. On the far side of the stall, on the road, <Subject 2>, exactly seven villagers, stand in a loose row facing him. As <Audio 1> begins, <Subject 1> (S1) raises his woven straw hat with a confident smile and speaks with lips precisely synced to <Audio 1>, delivering the line <d>[Chinese] 走江湖，闯江湖</d>, then lowers the hat as the camera pushes in slowly with small amplitude.\n[Shot 2] At 00:01.000, the camera cuts to a three-quarter medium shot of <Subject 1> facing the road. He sweeps his arm in a wide gesture across the ground stall toward <Subject 2> on the opposite side, the dust-stained cloth jacket shifting, his lips still synced to <Audio 1>, and delivers the line <d>[Chinese] 哪州哪县我不熟</d>. The customers nod and murmur softly while <Subject 3> continues tending their own stalls in the same row on both sides; he tucks the straw hat under his arm.\n[Shot 3] At 00:03.000, the came